WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:00.800
All right friends.

00:00.800 --> 00:02.680
So with that, we have covered a lot of stuff.

00:02.840 --> 00:05.080
So we have covered the customers and the products.

00:05.080 --> 00:09.960
And we are left with only one table where we have the transactions, the sales.

00:09.960 --> 00:13.000
And for the sales information we have only data from the CRM.

00:13.000 --> 00:14.720
We don't have anything from the ERP.

00:14.720 --> 00:16.320
So let's go and build it okay.

00:16.360 --> 00:18.400
So now I have all those informations.

00:18.400 --> 00:19.920
And now of course we have only one table.

00:19.920 --> 00:22.480
We don't have to do any integrations and so on.

00:22.480 --> 00:24.160
And now we have to answer the big question.

00:24.200 --> 00:26.440
Do we have here a dimension or facts.

00:26.440 --> 00:29.880
Well by looking to those details we can see transactions.

00:29.880 --> 00:31.000
We can see events.

00:31.000 --> 00:35.760
We have a lot of dates, informations we have as well a lot of measures and metrics.

00:35.800 --> 00:37.800
And as well we have a lot of IDs.

00:37.800 --> 00:40.360
So it is connecting multiple dimensions.

00:40.360 --> 00:43.640
And this is exactly a perfect setup for effects.

00:43.640 --> 00:46.840
So we're going to go and use those informations as effects.

00:46.840 --> 00:50.480
And of course as we learned the fact is connecting multiple dimensions.

00:50.720 --> 00:55.720
We have to present in these facts the surrogate keys that comes from the dimensions.

00:55.720 --> 01:01.530
So those two informations the product key and the customer ID those informations comes from the source

01:01.530 --> 01:02.050
system.

01:02.050 --> 01:05.930
And as we learned, we want to connect our data model using the surrogate keys.

01:05.970 --> 01:10.290
So what we're going to do, we're going to replace those two informations with the surrogate keys that

01:10.290 --> 01:11.250
we have generated.

01:11.250 --> 01:18.010
And in order to do that we have to go and join now the two dimensions in order to get the surrogate

01:18.050 --> 01:18.370
key.

01:18.410 --> 01:21.130
And we call this process of course data lookup.

01:21.130 --> 01:24.730
So we are joining the tables in order only to get one information.

01:24.730 --> 01:25.810
So let's go and do that.

01:25.850 --> 01:30.090
We will go with the left join of course not to lose any transaction.

01:30.090 --> 01:32.410
So first we're going to go and join it with the product key.

01:32.450 --> 01:36.210
Now of course in the silver layer we don't have any surrogate keys.

01:36.410 --> 01:37.890
We have it in the gold layer.

01:37.890 --> 01:43.730
So that means for the fact table we're going to be joining the silver layer together with the gold layer.

01:43.730 --> 01:47.410
So gold dots and then the dimension products.

01:47.450 --> 01:49.210
And I'm going to just call it PR.

01:49.330 --> 01:58.290
And we're going to join the SD using the product key together with the product number from the dimension.

01:58.290 --> 02:03.830
And now the only information that we need from the dimension is the key the surrogate key.

02:03.830 --> 02:07.470
So we're going to go over here and say product key.

02:07.510 --> 02:11.910
And what I'm going to do I'm going to go and remove this information from here because we don't need

02:11.910 --> 02:12.110
it.

02:12.150 --> 02:14.910
We don't need the original product key from the source system.

02:14.910 --> 02:19.030
We need the surrogate key that we have generated in our own in this data warehouse.

02:19.030 --> 02:21.710
So the same thing can happen as well for the customer.

02:22.270 --> 02:25.830
So goals dimension customer.

02:25.870 --> 02:30.790
Again we are doing here a lookup in order to get the information on SD.

02:30.950 --> 02:40.110
So we are joining using this ID over here equal to the customer ID because this is a customer ID and

02:40.110 --> 02:42.150
what we're going to do the same thing.

02:42.150 --> 02:45.590
We need the surrogate key the customer key.

02:45.630 --> 02:48.150
And we're going to delete the ID because we don't need it.

02:48.150 --> 02:49.350
Now we have the surrogate key.

02:49.350 --> 02:51.510
So now let's go and execute it.

02:51.510 --> 02:55.990
And now with that we have in our fact table the two keys from the dimensions.

02:55.990 --> 03:01.120
And now this can help us to connect the data model to connect the facts with the dimensions.

03:01.120 --> 03:02.480
So this is very necessary.

03:02.480 --> 03:04.360
Step building the fact table.

03:04.360 --> 03:07.680
You have to put the surrogate keys from the dimensions in the facts.

03:07.680 --> 03:09.760
So that was actually the hardest part.

03:09.800 --> 03:11.040
Building the facts.

03:11.080 --> 03:14.520
Now the next step all what you have to do is to go and give friendly names.

03:14.520 --> 03:17.840
So we're going to go over here and say order number.

03:18.320 --> 03:20.440
Then the surrogate keys are already friendly.

03:20.440 --> 03:23.960
So we're going to go over here and say this is the order date.

03:23.960 --> 03:27.040
And the next one is going to be shipping date.

03:28.000 --> 03:30.800
And then the next one due date.

03:30.920 --> 03:37.040
And the sales is going to be I'm going to say sales amount the quantity.

03:37.960 --> 03:40.600
And the final one is the price.

03:40.600 --> 03:43.640
So now let's go and execute it and look to the results.

03:43.800 --> 03:46.480
So now as you can see the columns looks very friendly.

03:46.480 --> 03:50.240
And now about the order of the columns we use the following schema.

03:50.240 --> 03:54.160
So first in the fact table we have all the surrogate keys from the dimensions.

03:54.280 --> 03:56.960
Then second we have all the dates.

03:56.960 --> 04:01.770
And at the end you group up all the measures and the metrics at the end of the facts.

04:01.810 --> 04:03.770
So that's it for the query, for the facts.

04:03.810 --> 04:05.730
Now we can go and build it.

04:05.730 --> 04:10.530
So we're going to say create a view gold in the gold layer.

04:10.610 --> 04:13.530
And this time we're going to use the facts underscore.

04:13.570 --> 04:15.290
And we're going to go and call it sales.

04:15.330 --> 04:16.930
And then don't forget about the --.

04:16.930 --> 04:17.930
So that's it.

04:17.930 --> 04:19.490
Let's go and create it.

04:19.530 --> 04:20.050
Perfect.

04:20.090 --> 04:21.410
Now we can see the facts.

04:21.410 --> 04:24.610
So with that we have three objects in the gold layer.

04:24.610 --> 04:26.610
We have two dimensions and one facts.

04:26.650 --> 04:31.090
And now of course the next step is that we're going to go and check the quality of the view.

04:31.610 --> 04:36.090
So let's have a simple select fact sales.

04:36.330 --> 04:38.890
So let's execute it now by checking the results.

04:38.890 --> 04:42.570
You can see it is exactly like the result from the query.

04:42.570 --> 04:44.130
And everything looks nice.

04:44.170 --> 04:44.410
Okay.

04:44.450 --> 04:49.650
So now one more trick that I usually do after building a fact is try to connect the whole data model

04:49.650 --> 04:51.170
in order to find any issues.

04:51.170 --> 04:52.130
So let's go and do that.

04:52.130 --> 04:55.730
We will do just simple left join with the dimensions.

04:55.730 --> 05:03.110
So gold dimension customers see and we will use the keys.

05:04.710 --> 05:08.190
And then we're going to say where customer key is null.

05:08.190 --> 05:09.630
So there is no matching.

05:10.030 --> 05:12.070
So let's go and execute it.

05:12.070 --> 05:14.830
And with that, as you can see in the results we are not getting anything.

05:14.830 --> 05:21.030
That means everything is matching perfectly and we can do as well the same thing with the products.

05:21.030 --> 05:32.030
So left join called them products P on product key and then we connect it with the fact product key.

05:32.070 --> 05:36.670
And then we can go and check the product key from the dimension like this.

05:36.670 --> 05:41.230
So we are checking whether we can connect the facts together with the dimension products.

05:41.230 --> 05:41.990
Let's go and check.

05:42.030 --> 05:44.430
And as you can see as well we are not getting anything.

05:44.430 --> 05:45.470
And this is all right.

05:45.470 --> 05:51.270
So with that we have now SQL codes that is tested and as well creating the gold layer.

05:51.310 --> 05:56.110
Now in the next step, as you know in our requirements we have to make clear documentations for the

05:56.110 --> 05:58.670
end users in order to use our data model.

05:58.670 --> 06:01.470
So let's go and draw a data model of the star schema.
